4NOV2024 The best performing tokenizer at the time of writing is 
ConformerUMM_2255_2375_TTS_ROPE recipe which operates at a 25hz token rate. 

These are the configs found in:
recipes/umm/conf/2024_Q2_conf_archives/conformer_tts_rope

In order to reduce inference time/memory pressure, we are trying to ablate tokenizers 
with lower frame rates of 20, 15 and 10hz.

The old tokenizer (ConformerUMM and ConformerUMM_TTS_ROPE) hard coded a lot of logic assuming
the input mel features were 100hz and the downsampling was 4x to 25 token rate. 

For these ablations I re-wrote the striding and conv module logic to support 20, 15 and 10hz. 
I also changed the mel feature sample rate to 120hz which is more easily divided into 20, 15 and 10 hz.

